            <ArticleTitle>[Aortocoronary shunting in unstable and early postinfarction angina pectoris due to lesion of a coronary artery].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>37-40</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Aortocoronary shunting was performed in 15 patients with unstable and early postinfarction angina pectoris. Coronarography revealed an isolated lesion of a coronary artery in all the patients. Two years after the operation the patients had no angina pectoris; no myocardial infarctions occurred.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
